; name: Chess knight
; group: Rotary axis
; description: A knight carved in the round from an STL model, in a Ø36 mm round blank on the rotary axis (along X; zero on the axis, at the −X end where the chuck is): the model is a 3D model shape, laid along the axis with its transforms, and turns with the stock, so a rotary repeat carves it from four sides — each roughed out with a Ø6 end mill down to the axis, then finished with a Ø6 ball nose. The knight stands with its base towards the chuck; a sprue on its head holds it at the tailstock end, to saw off after. Set the blank and the knight’s height with the variables, or load your own STL into the 3D model shape.

; 
